<%#
  Hamilton override of submit_form/_decline_form.

  Upstream asks "Notify the sender with the reason you declined", which names a
  side effect and never states the consequence. Nothing on the screen told a
  worker that this refuses to sign his employment agreement. The far more common
  intent behind tapping Decline is "I have a question", and upstream offered no
  way to act on that: the only exits were a 24px glyph and an invisible backdrop.

  So this partial states what declining does, says plainly that it is not a
  pause, points a worker with a question at Alex, and adds a labelled way back.

  Deliberately NOT discouraging. A worker is entitled to decline, and copy that
  pressured him out of it would be worse than the vague copy it replaced. Every
  sentence here is a fact about what the button does.

  Localised through I18n.locale rather than hardcoded, because ?lang=es must not
  land a Spanish signer on an English modal. Upstream's t(:decline) is reused for
  the header triggers, the modal title AND this button, so it cannot be
  redefined; these strings are local to the partial instead.

  Ruby stays on its own statement lines. A multi-line ternary inside an output
  tag is a syntax error and takes the whole page to a 500.

  Nothing in this comment may contain an ERB closing delimiter. The first one
  ends the comment, and every character after it renders to the signer as body
  text. An earlier revision of this very block illustrated the tag syntax
  literally and shipped "is a syntax error and takes the whole page to a 500."
  to the top of the decline modal, in both languages.
%>
<%
  es = I18n.locale.to_s.downcase.start_with?('es')

  consequence = if es
    'Rechazar le avisa a Hamilton que no vas a firmar este documento. No lo pausa ni lo guarda para después. Si solo tienes una pregunta, cierra esta ventana y llama o escríbele a Alex. Tu enlace sigue funcionando.'
  else
    'Declining tells Hamilton you will not sign this document. It does not pause it or save it for later. If you only have a question, close this box and call or message Alex. Your link keeps working.'
  end

  reason_label = es ? 'Motivo (obligatorio)' : 'Reason (required)'
  reason_hint  = es ? 'Dile a Alex por qué no vas a firmar' : 'Tell Alex why you are not signing this'
  decline_cta  = es ? 'Rechazar la firma' : 'Decline to sign'
  back_cta     = es ? 'Volver a firmar' : 'Go back to signing'
%>
<p class="hx-decline-note"><%= consequence %></p>
<%= form_for '', url: submit_form_decline_index_path(submitter.slug), method: :post do |f| %>
  <div class="form-control mt-4">
    <label class="label justify-start hx-decline-label" for="reason"><%= reason_label %></label>
    <%= f.text_area :reason, required: true, class: 'base-input w-full py-2', dir: 'auto', placeholder: reason_hint, rows: '4' %>
  </div>
  <toggle-submit dir="auto" class="form-control mt-4">
    <%= f.button button_title(title: decline_cta), class: 'base-button' %>
  </toggle-submit>
<% end %>
<%# Nested forms are invalid, so the way back lives outside the decline form.
    method="dialog" closes the modal with no request, same as the × glyph. %>
<form method="dialog" class="hx-decline-back">
  <button type="submit"><%= back_cta %></button>
</form>
